---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HomeHero from '../components/HomeHero.astro';
import ReadingPaths from '../components/ReadingPaths.astro';
import {articles,sections,sectionDescriptions,url} from '../lib/content';
const milestones=[['E51','A 3.1.3 daily workflow','Owner-accepted touch, stock Camera/Photos, complete power-off and photo reopening after cold power-on.'],['E44','Stock Camera, original providers','H1ISP and kernel AppleJPEG with unchanged Apple userland; 1600 × 1200 output from VGA acquisition.'],['E48','SD-free boot and recovery','eMMC/Tow-Boot staging with RTC recovery; protected media is checked separately from boot progress.'],['E54','The USB listener frontier','Enumeration and mux advance; first observed listener timing is diagnostic evidence, with ordinary pairing pending.']];
---
<Base>
<HomeHero/>
<section class="scope-strip"><span class="mono">THE STUDY</span><p>Original 1.1.4 and 3.1.3 userspace. Adapted XNU. An A64 PinePhone. <br/><span>A preserved reference in emulation, and a native port examined one boundary at a time.</span></p><a href={url('articles/three-machines/')}>Understand the three environments ↗</a></section>
<section class="home-section discoveries"><div class="section-intro"><span class="section-number">01 — FINDINGS</span><h2>What the experiments <br/>actually establish.</h2><p>Four physical milestones. Each has a method, an observation and a limit.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('evidence/')}>Open the evidence ledger →</a></div><div class="finding-list">{milestones.map(([id,title,desc])=><a class="finding" href={url('evidence/'+id+'/')}><span class="evidence-id">{id}<i class="line"/></span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{desc}</p></div><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>)}<p class="limits-note"><strong>THE PUBLISHED BOUNDARY</strong>The 7E18 daily workflow is accepted by hand. Pairing, stock rotation, GPU, audio, network and telephony remain open. Output geometry and measured preview throughput have separate limits. Explore the <a href="/ios/status/">capability status →</a></p></div></section>
<section class="home-section chapter-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-number">02 — THE ATLAS</span><h2>Read the system in layers.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={url('library/')}>All {articles.length} chapters →</a></div><div class="domain-list">{sections.map((section,i)=><a href={url('library/#'+section.toLowerCase())} class="domain-row" data-domain={section}><span class="domain-no">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{section}</h3><p>{sectionDescriptions[section]}</p><span class="domain-count">{articles.filter(a=>a.section===section).length} chapters <span>↗</span></span></a>)}</div></section>
<ReadingPaths/>
<section class="correction-feature"><span class="section-number">RESEARCH IS ALSO REVISION</span><h2>The useful discoveries <br/>included being wrong.</h2><div><p>A modeled CPU bit changed a physical atomic operation. UART logging consumed a USB address deadline. A fixed delay failed to establish service readiness.</p><a class="button light" href={url('paper/#8-case-studies-useful-disagreements-and-failures')}>Read the bug case studies <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
</Base>
